1:# taskboard
2:
3:A keyboard-first task board for the terminal, built with [Textual](https://textual.textualize.io/).
4:Run it in a borderless terminal window, pin it on top, and it works as a desktop widget: ten
5:views over one JSON board, with optional team sync through a shared folder.
6:
7:<p align="center">
8:  <img src="docs/taskboard-ambient.gif" width="760" alt="taskboard — the lanes view, live"><br>
9:  <img src="docs/taskboard-gantt.svg" width="380" alt="gantt — the whole board on a window fitted to the open work">
10:  <img src="docs/taskboard-kanban.png" width="380" alt="kanban — every task in its phase column"><br>
11:  <img src="docs/taskboard-agenda.png" width="380" alt="agenda — every due date on one shared axis">
12:  <img src="docs/taskboard-lanes.png" width="380" alt="lanes — one panel per project"><br>
13:  <sub>Renders of the seeded demo board. The gantt is current; the other images predate this
14:  release's colour changes.</sub>
15:</p>
16:
17:## What it is
18:
19:- **A widget, not a window.** No borders: every view commits with rules, and it reflows to
20:  whatever size the terminal gives it.
21:- **Ten views** over the same tasks — lanes, agenda, gantt, kanban, focus, chains, flow, standup,
22:  people, setup — each one key away.
23:- **One file.** Your board is a single JSON file in your home directory; nothing goes to a
24:  server.
25:- **Optional team mode.** Point it at a shared folder and each person's board syncs there;
26:  teammates' cards show up read-only.
27:
28:## Requirements
29:
30:- Python **3.12 or newer** (`requires-python = ">=3.12"`).
31:- **Windows first.** It is built and used on Windows; opening raw image files uses
32:  `os.startfile`, which is Windows-only. The clipboard code has macOS and Linux branches, but
33:  those platforms are not tested here.
34:- Built and verified against **Textual 8.2.8 / rich 15.0.0** (pinned in `requirements.txt`).
35:  The install pulls in every runtime dependency (`textual`, `tzdata`, `pillow`,
36:  `textual-image`).
37:
38:## Install
39:
40:Clone the repository, then install it as a command.
41:
42:```powershell
43:git clone https://github.com/jav201/taskboard.git
44:cd taskboard
45:```
46:
47:**With pipx (recommended).** pipx gives the app its own environment and puts `taskboard` on
48:your PATH:
49:
50:```powershell
51:python -m pip install --user pipx
52:python -m pipx ensurepath        # then open a new terminal so PATH updates
53:pipx install .
54:```
55:
56:To update after pulling new code: `pipx reinstall taskboard`. This installs the newest
57:Textual; the exact versions the app is verified against are pinned in `requirements.txt`
58:(see [`RUN.md`](RUN.md)).
59:
60:**With pip.** `pip install --user .` installs the same `taskboard` command. If the shell says
=== table lines ===
83:| `1` | **Lanes** | One panel per project with its load and due work; `Tab` switches the grid (default) and the classic waves layout |
84:| `2` | **Agenda** | Every dated task on one shared day axis, by urgency |
85:| `3` | **Gantt** | The whole board on a window fitted to the open work, with a date ruler on top |
86:| `4` | **Kanban** | Every task in its phase column; `Tab` cycles grouped, matrix and lanes layouts |
87:| `5` | **Focus** | Pinned tasks and pinned projects, in five layouts (`Tab`) |
88:| `6` | **Chains** | The chain map: who waits on whom, per project — the ready/waits/late marks, the critical chain, and the per-chain `dates` rule on screen |
89:| `7` | **Flow** | Read-only: time in phase, a phase × week heatmap, weekly throughput |
90:| `8` | **Standup** | Team mode: one row per teammate — load, top task, sync age |
91:| `9` | **People** | Team mode: one lane per teammate; their cards are read-only |
92:| `0` | **Setup** | Team configuration, edited in the app with live health checks |
108:| `?` | Help | Per-view help (usage, legend, example, keys); `m` there for the full map |
109:| `;` | More | Toggle the key bar's layer |
110:| `q` | Quit | Quit |
111:| `1`–`6`, `7`–`9`, `0` | Views | See [Views](#views) |
112:| `↑` `↓` / `k` `j` | Move | Move the selection in the order the view draws |
113:| `←` `→` / `h` `l` | Across | Move between columns (kanban) |
114:| `Enter` | Details | Every field of the selected task; its links can be changed there |
115:| `a` / `e` | Add / Edit | Add a task / edit the selected one in the full-screen editor |
116:| `d` / `Delete` | Delete | Delete the selected task (asks first) |
117:| `L` | Link | Make the selected task wait on another one (a picker; on the gantt, a link mode) |
118:| `M` | Milestone | Make the selected task a milestone — one date, its due — or a task again |
119:| `[` `]` | Phase | Move the selected task one phase back / forward |
120:| `!` | Priority | Cycle low → normal → high |
121:| `b` | Blocked | Mark an outside block (`▲`) on the task, or clear it |
122:| `+` `=` / `-` | Due | Due date one day later / earlier — what waits on it follows by the project's rule |
123:| `m` | Chain | Re-apply the last date move under the next mode (stay / push / together) |
124:| `u` | Undo | Undo the last quick change |
125:| `x` / `v` | Archive | Archive or unarchive / show archived tasks |
126:| `X` | Purge done | Archive all finished work that has no completion date (asks first) |
127:| `t` / `T` | Pin | Pin the task / its whole project (Focus view) |
128:| `o` / `i` | Links / Images | Open the task's http(s) links / view its images |
129:| `p` / `P` | Projects | Add a project / manage projects |
130:| `f` | Phases | Add, rename, reorder or delete the board's phases |
131:| `s` `g` `z` | Kanban | Sort, group, collapse the last phase |
132:| `F` / `/` / `esc` | Focus, filter | Kanban and gantt: focus one project / filter tasks / clear |
133:| `Tab` | Layout | Cycle the layouts of kanban, focus and lanes |
134:| `R` / `S` | Present / Standup | Present the selected task's project (gantt + brief, export SVG+PNG) / show the week's standup |
135:| `I` | Templates | Insert a process template (a named chain of tasks) into the selected task's project |
136:| `c` | Clocks | Choose the ribbon's two city clocks |
137:| `space` / `ctrl+s` | Setup | In Setup: toggle a control / save; `Enter` edits a row, `a` / `x` add or remove a row, `Tab` changes section, `esc` discards |
277:| `board.json` | Your board: projects, tasks, settings |
278:| `board.json.corrupt` | A copy of an unreadable board, kept before the app starts empty |
279:| `history.jsonl` | One line per phase move and per added task — the Flow view reads it |
280:| `images/<task id>/` | Pasted images, as plain files |
281:| `reports/` | HTML reports and the presentation's SVG + PNG exports |
290:| `taskboard` | Run the app on `~/.taskboard/board.json` |
291:| `taskboard --board PATH` | Run it on another board file |
292:| `taskboard --report [PROJECT]` | Write a report and exit |
